cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use potsynth in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "potsynth: fast synthesis of potential-field models at scattered points"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Alken
    given-names: Patrick
  - family-names: Burchill
    given-names: Johnathan
version: 0.1.0
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/pa345/potsynth"
abstract: >-
  potsynth evaluates spherical harmonic models of internal potential fields
  (geomagnetic and gravity models) at large numbers of scattered points. After a
  one-off set-up, the cost per point does not depend on the maximum degree of the
  model. It provides a C library with a Python interface.
keywords:
  - spherical harmonics
  - geomagnetism
  - gravity field
  - crustal field
  - NUFFT
